      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T20:55:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "LeanParser places inline @[...] attributes in both decl.attributes() and decl.signatureLines(), so scanning both here counts hidden or control characters inside an inline attribute twice. That triggers spurious raw lineDiff fallbacks on intact inline attributes, and can mask a dropped hidden character elsewhere in the declaration (for example, a trimmed doc-comment edge control char or malformed deriving line) when the duplicate count cancels out the missing character. Only scan standalone attributes not already present in signatureLines() (or drop the decl.attributes() loop so standalone attributes with hidden chars fall back to raw lineDiff).",
      "range": {
